@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
left to right direction
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam classBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classBorderColor #64748B
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF7ED
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
title Ontology v0.11 — Module–Skill teaching focus and difficulty
class Occupation {
 code : String
 name : String
 jobZone : Integer
 interestRealistic : Float [0,1]
 interestInvestigative : Float [0,1]
 interestArtistic : Float [0,1]
 interestSocial : Float [0,1]
 interestEnterprising : Float [0,1]
 interestConventional : Float [0,1]
}
class TargetRole {
 code : String
 name : String
 scope : String
}
class Level {
 code : String
 name : String
 rank : Integer
 attainmentRule = ALL_MANDATORY_SKILLS
}
class Competency {
 name : String
 description : String
 attainmentRule = ALL_MEMBER_SKILLS_AT_OWNING_LEVEL
}
class MicroSkill {
 name : String
 definition : String
}
class LearningModule {
 title : String
 moduleType : String
 contentUri : String
 contentType : String
 contentVersion : String
 duration : Integer (minutes > 0)
 price : Float (VND > 0)
}
Occupation "1" --> "1..*" TargetRole : HAS_ROLE
TargetRole "1" --> "1..*" Level : HAS_LEVEL
Level "1" -up-> "1..*" Competency : HAS_COMPETENCY
Competency "0..*" --> "1..*" MicroSkill : HAS_SKILL
Level "0..*" --> "1..*" MicroSkill : REQUIRES_SKILL
LearningModule "1..*" -up-> "1..*" MicroSkill : TEACHES
note on link
TEACHES relationship properties (both required):
teachingFocus: PRIMARY | SUPPORTING | INCIDENTAL
difficultyLevel: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH
Independent per Module-Skill pair, not node fields.
Example MOD-FOCUS-CORE01-HIGH:
MS-CORE01: PRIMARY / HIGH
MS-CORE02: SUPPORTING / MEDIUM
MS-CORE03: INCIDENTAL / LOW (no gap-closure credit)
Difficulty does not follow numeric gap or role title.
end note
MicroSkill --> MicroSkill : HAS_SKILL_PREREQUISITE
note bottom of MicroSkill
REQUIRES_SKILL: requiredScore [0,1], isMandatory.
HAS_SKILL_PREREQUISITE: requiredScore [0,1].
end note
note top of Competency
Owned by one Level.
All member skills PASS under that Level's requirements
=> Competency ACHIEVED.
No independent score or assessment.
end note
note bottom of Level
Each Level has its own skill requirements and competencies.
Skill sets may differ across Levels of the same role.
A Competency member must be required by its owning Level.
end note
note bottom of LearningModule
TEACHES stores teachingFocus + difficultyLevel.
Each Module has exactly ONE PRIMARY skill.
Other links may be SUPPORTING or INCIDENTAL.
INCIDENTAL is context, not a taught outcome.
Neither enum proves learner mastery.
A Module teaches one or more Skills.
A Skill can have several teaching Modules.
Providers are alternatives, not all mandatory.
Select learning content through missing skills.
Check content depth against the selected Level.
Skill prerequisites determine learning readiness.
Module completion does not automatically prove skill mastery.
end note
note top of Occupation
Each TargetRole has one owning Occupation.
Repeated reported titles use distinct role IDs per Occupation.
Shared metadata: id, version, status, reviewStatus,
reviewedBy?, reviewedAt?
end note
@enduml
